  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">R&#xe9;ponse multisectorielle d&apos;urgence au profit des populations d&#xe9;plac&#xe9;es dans la r</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project forms part of Oxfam&apos;s humanitarian intervention strategy for Niger and is aligned with the strategic objectives set out by Niger&apos;s government in its Support Plan for 2022. Its focus is on saving lives, mitigating hardship experienced by communities (specifically displaced persons and their vulnerable hosts), as well as safeguarding the human rights and dignity of those affected by the security and food crises. The emergency response component will provide an integrated response to meet immediate needs life -saving needs for food assistance, Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) and Protection for 8,400 displaced people, refugees and host communities (1,200 highly vulnerable households) in Tillab&#xe9;ri region. In view of the food crisis in Niger, Oxfam has updated its humanitarian response plan to meet the urgent needs of affected households, with consideration for the insecurity experienced by displaced persons in the places where they live. The project encompasses Food Security, WASH and Protection, all of which are recognised as Oxfam areas of expertise. Quality standards and requirements will be met and implemented with assistance from the partner organisation.</narrative>
  </description>
